{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0291-forecasting-number-of-corner-kicks-taken.md", "equation": "Eq. 1 (DCP): Y = Σ_{i=1}^N X_i, N ~ Poisson(λ), X_i i.i.d. discrete. Eq. 2 (pgf): G_Y(s) = exp{Σ_{i=1}^∞ α_i λ (s^i − 1)}, Σα_i = 1. NB as DCP (logarithmic cluster sizes, Quenouille 1949): p_X(x) = [−1/log(1−p)] (p^x/x), x ≥ 1; adopted parameterisation (Gelman et al. 1995): p_Y(y) = C(y+κ−1, y) (λ/(λ+κ))^y (κ/(λ+κ))^κ; E[Y] = λ, Var[Y] = λ + λ²/κ, D = 1 + λ/κ; Poisson limit as κ → ∞. Geometric-Poisson (Özel & Inal 2010): p_Y(0) = e^{−λ}; p_Y(y) = e^{−λ} Σ_{k=1}^y (λ^k/k!) C(y−1, k−1) θ^k (1−θ)^{y−k}; E[Y] = λ/θ, Var[Y] = λ(2−θ)/θ², D = (2−θ)/θ; pgf exp{−λ[1 − (1−θ)s/(1−θs)]}. Margin removal: multiplicative p_i = π_i/π; odds ratio OR = p_i(1−π_i)/(π_i(1−p_i)), p_i = π_i/(OR + π_i − OR·π_i); Shin p_i = [√(z² + 4(1−z)π_i²/π) − z]/[2(1−z)] with z iterated from 0; power p_i = π_i^{1/k}, Σ p_i = 1. Cross-market loss: (p_H−p'_H)² + (p_D−p'_D)² + (p_L−p'_L)² minimised over (λ̂₁, λ̂₂) to get TG_i ...", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9200}
